This chapter shares only companion, Speaker and converse.

Use the foundation chapter.

A companion has an actor (text), a question (text), a response (text), an identity (text), a profile (text) and a voice (text).
There is a companion called Speaker whose actor is "" and whose question is "" and whose response is "" and whose identity is "" and whose profile is "" and whose voice is "".

Use the maps and characters chapters.

To work out the spoken words (text) of a question (text):
  Let the wording be the question in lower case.
  Let the spoken be "".
  Let the quoted be no.
  Let the position be 0.
  Repeat the length of the wording times:
    Add 1 to the position.
    Let the mark be letter the position of the wording or else "".
    If the mark is one of """", "“" or "”":
      If the quoted is yes:
        Set the quoted to no.
      Otherwise:
        Set the quoted to yes.
      Set the spoken to "{the spoken} ".
    Otherwise if the quoted is no:
      If the mark is "’":
        Set the mark to "'".
      If "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'" contains the mark:
        Set the spoken to "{the spoken}{the mark}".
      Otherwise:
        Set the spoken to "{the spoken} ".
  The answer is the spoken.

Let the intensifiers always be a list of "so", "really", "very", "truly", "too" and "extremely".
Let the denials always be a list of "not", "never", "don't", "dont" and "no".

The tone cues are tone, in that order:
  "hate" has "firm".
  "stupid" has "firm".
  "idiot" has "firm".
  "kill" has "firm".
  "ugly" has "firm".
  "loser" has "firm".
  "rude" has "firm".
  "are mean" has "firm".
  "you're mean" has "firm".
  "youre mean" has "firm".
  "shut up" has "firm".
  "hurt you" has "firm".
  "love you" has "warm".
  "date me" has "warm".
  "thank" has "warm".
  "thanks" has "warm".
  "kind" has "warm".
  "kind of" has "".
  "friend" has "warm".
  "nice" has "warm".
  "flirt" has "warm".
  "kiss" has "warm".
  "beautiful" has "warm".
  "cute" has "warm".

To work out the telling words (list of text) of a question (text):
  Let the telling (list of text) be an empty list of text.
  For each word in the words of (the spoken words of the question):
    If the word is not in the intensifiers:
      Add the word to the telling.
  The answer is the telling.

To work out the cue (text) of a sentence (list of text) at a place (number):
  Let the word be item the place of the sentence or else "".
  Let the following be item (the place + 1) of the sentence or else "".
  Let the before be item (the place - 1) of the sentence or else "".
  If the before is in the denials:
    The answer is "".
  Let the phrase cue be the tone cues for "{the word} {the following}".
  If the phrase cue is not nothing:
    The answer is the phrase cue's tone.
  Let the word cue be the tone cues for the word.
  If the word cue is not nothing:
    The answer is the word cue's tone.
  The answer is "".

To work out the attitude (text) of a question (text):
  Let the telling be the telling words of the question.
  Let the mood be "".
  Let the place be 0.
  Repeat the number of items in the telling times:
    Add 1 to the place.
    Depending on the cue of the telling at the place:
      For "firm":
        The answer is "firm".
      For "warm":
        Set the mood to "warm".
  The answer is the mood.

To work out the plain wording (text) of a question (text):
  Let the wording be the question in lower case.
  Let the plain be "".
  Let the position be 0.
  Repeat the length of the wording times:
    Add 1 to the position.
    Let the mark be letter the position of the wording or else " ".
    If the mark is "é":
      Set the mark to "e".
    If "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz" does not contain the mark:
      Set the mark to " ".
    Set the plain to "{the plain}{the mark}".
  The answer is the plain.

To work out the topic words (list of text) of a question (text):
  Let the topics (list of text) be the words of (the plain wording of the question).
  For each word in the words of (the plain wording of the question):
    If the word ends with "s" and the length of the word is more than 3:
      Add the first (the length of the word - 1) letters of the word to the topics.
  The answer is the topics.

To work out the topic phrasing (text) of a question (text):
  Let the joined be (the words of (the plain wording of the question)) joined with " ".
  The answer is " {the joined} ".

The keywords are topic, in that order:
  "pokedex" has "pokedex".
  "parcel" has "parcel".
  "badge" has "badge".
  "win" has "badge".
  "starter" has "starter".
  "partner" has "starter".
  "grass" has "wild".
  "wild" has "wild".
  "pokemon" has "pokemon".
  "oak" has "oak".
  "professor" has "oak".
  "grandpa" has "oak".
  "home" has "home".
  "miss" has "home".
  "missed" has "home".
  "battle" has "battle".
  "strong" has "battle".
  "rock" has "rock".
  "gym" has "rock".
  "brock" has "brock".
  "light" has "light".
  "year" has "light".

Let the topic order always be a list of "pokedex", "parcel", "badge", "starter", "wild", "pokemon", "oak", "home", "battle", "rock", "brock", "light" and "greeting".

To work out the topics raised (list of text) by a question (text):
  Let the raised (list of text) be an empty list of text.
  For each word in the topic words of the question:
    Let the keyword be the keywords for the word.
    If the keyword is not nothing:
      Add the keyword's topic to the raised.
  Add "greeting" to the raised.
  The answer is the raised.

To work out the progress (text) on a topic (text):
  If the topic is one of "parcel", "pokedex" or "oak":
    If Journey's dex is 1:
      The answer is "delivered".
    If Journey's parcel is 1:
      The answer is "carried".
  If the topic is one of "starter" or "pokemon" and Journey's starter is not "":
    The answer is "chosen".
  If the topic is "badge" and Journey's badge is 1:
    The answer is "earned".
  The answer is "".

To work out the topic line (text) of a speaker (text) on a topic (text):
  Let the progressed be the topic replies for "{the speaker}:{the topic}:{the progress on the topic}".
  If the progressed is not nothing:
    The answer is the progressed's line.
  Let the general be the topic replies for "{the speaker}:{the topic}".
  If the general is not nothing:
    The answer is the general's line.
  The answer is "".

To work out the fitting line (text) of a speaker (text) for a raised (list of text):
  For each topic in the topic order:
    If the topic is in the raised:
      Let the line be the topic line of the speaker on the topic.
      If the line is not "":
        The answer is the line.
  The answer is "".

To work out the filled line (text) of a template (text):
  Let the filled be "".
  Let the rest be the template.
  While the rest is not "":
    Let the mark be letter 1 of the rest or else "".
    Let the value be the mark.
    If the rest starts with "[trainer]":
      Set the mark to "[trainer]".
      Set the value to Journey's trainer.
    Otherwise if the rest starts with "[starter]":
      Set the mark to "[starter]".
      Set the value to Journey's starter.
    Otherwise if the rest starts with "[rival starter]":
      Set the mark to "[rival starter]".
      Set the value to Journey's rival starter.
    Set the filled to "{the filled}{the value}".
    Set the rest to the last (the length of the rest - the length of the mark) letters of the rest.
  The answer is the filled.

Let the story requests always be a list of "your story", "about yourself", "who are you", "your past", "your background" and "tell me about you".

To converse with a guest (text) about a question (text):
  Set Speaker's actor to the guest.
  Set Speaker's identity to "".
  Set Speaker's profile to "".
  Set Speaker's voice to "".
  Set Speaker's question to the question.
  Set Speaker's response to "I don't know enough about that to say. What else would you like to talk about?".
  Let the nearby column be the conversation column.
  Let the nearby row be the conversation row.
  If the guest is "":
    Set Speaker's response to "There is no one here to talk to.".
    Stop.
  Let the address be "{Journey's place}:{the nearby column},{the nearby row}:{the guest}".
  Let the character address be the address.
  If the address is "Blue's House:6,4:Daisy":
    Set the character address to "Blue's House:2,3:Daisy".
  Let the character be the character portraits for the character address.
  If the character is not nothing:
    Set Speaker's identity to the character address, except:
      Use "Oak's Lab:4,3:Rival" for "Route 22:25,5:Route 22 Rival".
    Set Speaker's profile to the character's background.
    Set Speaker's voice to the character's voice.
    If the address is "Home:5,4:Mom":
      Set Speaker's profile to "Mom raised {Journey's trainer} {the character's background}".
    If the character address is "Blue's House:2,3:Daisy":
      Set Speaker's profile to "Daisy knows her brother and {Journey's trainer} {the character's background}".
    Let the mood be the attitude of the question.
    If the mood is "firm":
      Set Speaker's response to "{the guest}: {the character's firm response}".
      Stop.
    Let the phrasing be the topic phrasing of the question.
    For each phrase in the story requests:
      If the phrasing contains " {the phrase} ":
        Set Speaker's response to "{the guest}: {the character's story}".
        Stop.
    If the mood is "warm":
      Set Speaker's response to "{the guest}: {the character's warm response}".
      Stop.
  Let the raised be the topics raised by the question.
  Let the line be the fitting line of the character address for the raised.
  If the line is "":
    Set the line to the fitting line of the guest for the raised.
  If the line is not "":
    Set Speaker's response to the filled line of the line.
